This pull request updates the Lambda configuration to use a dedicated application database user (db_app_user) instead of the master database user, and disables automatic log group creation for the Lambdas. The changes improve security by following the principle of least privilege and prepare the infrastructure for environments where a dedicated DB user is available.

Database user improvements:

Added a new local variable db_app_user in locals.tf that selects the application DB user from Aurora state if available, falling back to the master username otherwise.
Updated both policy_graph_ingest_lambda and soap_verification_lambda modules in lambda.tf to use local.db_app_user for the db_user environment variable and in RDS IAM policy resource ARNs, replacing the previous use of the master username. [1] [2] [3] [4]
Lambda logging configuration:

Changed create_log_group to false for both Lambda modules, indicating that log group creation is now managed elsewhere. [1] [2]
