Unconditional imports fail when log groups do not exist
An import block is not a no-op when the remote object is absent: OpenTofu will fail planning if this log group has not already been created, before the create_log_group = true resource can create it. Because these blocks run unconditionally for every workspace, a fresh environment or a Lambda that has not yet been invoked cannot deploy; use one-time imports for known existing groups or make the import behavior conditional.

